  "id": "COMPOUND:31899 - PROTEIN:5849",
  "verbalization": "Nortoxiferine, dihydro- is linked to A549 through a series of target relationships, all ultimately converging on the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit is targeted by multiple compounds, including Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone, and Picrinine, all of which have A549 as their target. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same subunit suggests a potential mechanism involving the proteasome, a key player in protein degradation and cellular homeostasis. The integration of these pathways implies that Nortoxiferine, dihydro- may exert its effects through the proteasome, potentially modulating cellular processes in A549 cells. The evidence supports a role for Nortoxiferine, dihydro- in influencing the proteasome, which in turn affects A549 cell function, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
